roms
target
# `SUITES=.test-suites make test-external` — the external ROMs kept out of
# `target/`, which is what CI does so the compiler cache does not swallow them.
.test-suites
node_modules

# **The ROOT `Cargo.lock` is tracked and must stay so**: this crate ships
# binaries, CI and `docs/quickstart.md` both build `--locked` against it, and an
# ignored lockfile means a dependency bump never shows up in `git status`. A
# bare `Cargo.lock` line used to sit here, inherited from upstream, while the
# file was committed anyway. Lockfiles BELOW the root belong to crates that are
# deliberately not workspace members (`platform/m5paper`,
# `third_party/blip_buf-nostd`) and are build artefacts — they stay ignored.
**/Cargo.lock
!/Cargo.lock

**/*.a
**/*.gb
**/*.gbc
**/*.gbsave

# ...but the vendored dmg-acid2 test ROM must be tracked (MIT-licensed, see
# third_party/dmg-acid2/LICENSE). It is prebuilt because upstream ships source only.
!third_party/dmg-acid2/dmg-acid2.gb
# and the GBSelfTest cartridge, which is MIT and ours to redistribute; see
# third_party/gbselftest/README.md and tools/fetch-gbselftest.sh
!third_party/gbselftest/gbselftest.gb

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

main_static

.DS_Store
log
NOTES
# The conformance runner is Python; keep its bytecode cache out of the tree.
__pycache__/

# Learned guidance is a run artefact, true only of the save it was played
# from — see scenarios/README.md.
scenarios/guidance/
scenarios/*/guidance/

# The Pewter chain's derived save states. **Never committed**: a Game Boy save
# state is a dump of the machine's RAM and VRAM, so it carries the cartridge's
# own tile data — game content, under the same rule as every other asset here.
# Every one of them is reproducible from a fresh cartridge by playing the chain
# forward; see docs/agent/pewter-chain.md.
scenarios/pewter/states/

# Secrets never belong in the tree. Nothing here reads a dotenv file today;
# this is the guard for the day something does.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Doc-preview artefacts. `AGENTS.md` describes rendering a page through
# GitHub's own /markdown API to check it before committing; the output of that
# is scratch and must not ship.
.preview/
*.preview.html
readme-*.html
